      "side": 1,
      "message": "sure. I did consider doing that at one point, but ended up not doing that because I  wanted to reuse the same byte buffer for each read (to hopefully gain some cache locality).\nIn order to make this method a method of Poll entry, I would either make the `PollEntry` non-static or stick each PollEntry an exclusive buffer.\nI don\u0027t like the former because it would \"taint\" the PollEntry abstraction by making it a non-pure structure (PollEntry relies on global state; PollEntry assumes exclusive hold of the mReadBuffer), so I\u0027ll take the latter choice. This means potentially worse cache locality, but probably not a big hit anyway given the size of the readbuffer is not large (4K).",
